WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:06.920
Journalist Friday Olokor is getting ready
for an historic moment: Nigeria’s first-ever

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:13.280
presidential debate, broadcast live on all
major channels across the country.

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:16.299
But minutes before the start, speculation
is building.

00:00:16.299 --> 00:00:18.480
Will the president himself show up?

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:25.250
"It has never happened that an incumbent will
come and appear at a live debate.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:26.990
It has never happened.

00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:35.820
But if President Muhammadu Buhari appears
for this debate, he will make history and

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:44.750
will enter into the nation's annals of positive
politics."

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:47.290
The event venue is filling up – but no sign

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:48.829
of Buhari.

00:00:48.829 --> 00:00:51.239
Organizers say he promised to be here.

00:00:51.239 --> 00:00:56.860
Atiku Abubakar, presidential candidate for
Nigeria's biggest opposition party, the PDP,

00:00:56.860 --> 00:01:22.520
has already arrived – but now refuses
to go on stage.

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:28.060
We came here for a Presidential debate, not
a candidacy debate, and I, Atiku Abubakar

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:32.690
cannot challenge or question an administration
where the man at the helm of the affairs of

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:37.170
the nation is not present to defend himself
or his policies.

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:40.590
So, the podiums remain empty.

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:44.640
The PDP and Buhari's APC party are the two
biggest parties in Nigeria.

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:48.750
They're also the only democratic parties to
ever rule the country.

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:54.940
"They have just simply announced their exit
from governance."

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:59.240
"Pride always comes before the fall.

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:04.200
And every time you believe that you have no
need to tell the people what you are going

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:09.890
to do – it means that you are not there
to serve them in the first place."

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:11.670
President Buhari is not known for being a

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:14.360
talented speaker.

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:18.220
The 75-year old has also suffered from health
problems over the last few years.

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:22.950
Many Nigerians believe he dodged the debate
after an embarassing performance at his last

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:25.450
live appearance at a town hall meeting on
Wednesday.

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:29.540
There, he appeared anxious and struggled to
answer questions.

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:31.830
"Well, uh.

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:34.569
I honestly cannot remember.

00:02:34.569 --> 00:02:35.569
Uh."

00:02:35.569 --> 00:02:40.430
At the end of the presidential debate, Friday
Olokor is satisfied – despite the limited

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:41.430
attendance.

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:46.430
The other candidates did a good job, the journalist
says, talking about the burning topics in

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:49.650
Nigeria: education, the struggling economy,
and security.

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:55.370
Maybe, Olokor says, some of Nigeria's poltiical
underdogs might have a real chance now.

